7592186501141 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine ${f}^{″}(t)$ given that $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{t} \\\\ {e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -2{t}^{6}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}^{″}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501141 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0cc15b80-72fe-59a5-9238-583abab2565e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501141 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{1-2t})\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{t}^{6})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}} \\\\ -2{e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -12{t}^{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{″}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-2{e}^{1-2t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-12{t}^{5})\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{{t}^{3/2}} \\\\ 4{e}^{1-2t} \\\\ -60{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501147 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501147 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501147 #edb/ref 1069 "q-349464" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501147 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501147 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-7t+1,\\,8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501147 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "19691404-0bb9-5165-a3cc-ce9a79557b1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501147 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=3{t}^{4}-7t+1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{3}-7.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12{t}^{3}-7,\\,8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501155 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501116 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501155 #edb/ref 1069 "q-50377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501155 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501155 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨4t-10,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501155 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2bf645e6-f706-50ea-8450-5ddbc0499160" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501155 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4t-10,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{3}{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\frac{3}{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501172 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501172 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501172 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501172 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2}\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501172 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "66e3887f-e0ed-593b-b271-ae704cd5f2f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501172 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501126 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1069 "q-350227" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that  $f(t)=2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)\\,i-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+\\frac{6}{t}\\,k,$   what is ${f}^{′}(1)?$\n\n${f}^{′}(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$j\\,\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$k$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87416abb-dad9-5afe-bb9d-e8fcd5a9095c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501190 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t))\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{6}{t})\\,k \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3t)+2)\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-\\frac{6}{{t}^{2}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(1),$ we substitute $t=1$ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(1) & =(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot 1)+2)\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)\\,j-\\frac{6}{{1}^{2}}\\,k \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\,i-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡1\\,j-6\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501194 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501096 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501194 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75033" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501194 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501194 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨4{t}^{3}-t,\\,7t-3{t}^{4}⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501194 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b01d0b7-5c1a-5382-b422-a24594a7e8ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501194 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=4{t}^{3}-t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =12{t}^{2}-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=7t-3{t}^{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =7-12{t}^{3} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-36{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨24t,\\,-36{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501223 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501223 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501223 #edb/ref 1069 "q-349466" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501223 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501223 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),\\,{t}^{2}+4t⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501223 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6495e61-0973-5b35-994b-13978ddf3f2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501223 #edb/ref 1074 "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)={t}^{2}+4t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=2t+4.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),\\,2t+4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501238 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501040 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186501238 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186501067 #edb/ref 